---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const pageTitle = "Interactive Kitchen Safety Tools & Diagnostics | IsItKitchenSafe";
const pageDescription = "Explore our free, evidence-based kitchen safety tools: Induction Cooktop EMF & Pacemaker Safety Modeler, Microwave Radiation Leakage Evaluator, Slow Cooker Glaze Leaching & Spore Simulator, Air Fryer Acrylamide Calculator, Water Filter Efficiency Analyzer, Sous Vide Modeler, and AI Diagnostics.";

const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: 'Tools' }
];

const faqs = [
  {
    question: "Are IsItKitchenSafe tools free to use?",
    answer: "Yes, 100% free and open-access. Our tools do not require any signup, app installation, or user account."
  },
  {
    question: "How does the Induction Cooktop EMF Radiation & Cardiac Pacemaker Safety Modeler work?",
    answer: "The modeler calculates intermediate frequency (20–50 kHz) magnetic flux density (in μT and mG) generated by planar induction coils against ICNIRP (1998/2010) public exposure guidelines and IEC/EN 62233 standards. It factors in pan base ferromagnetic coupling efficiency, pot-to-coil diameter mismatch, off-center placement, and power levels (up to 3.7 kW boost). Using near-field power law distance attenuation, it predicts EMI sensing disruption risks for patients with bipolar or unipolar cardiac pacemakers and ICDs."
  },
  {
    question: "How does the Microwave Radiation Leakage & Door Gasket Evaluator calculate risk?",
    answer: "The evaluator implements RF wave propagation physics and transmission line equations across 2.45 GHz electromagnetic fields. It models quarter-wave (λ/4) choke cavity impedance matching, door gap dilation from warped latches or hinge sag, and gasket compression degradation against federal FDA 21 CFR § 1030.10 limits (1.0 mW/cm² new, 5.0 mW/cm² lifetime at 5 cm). It applies inverse-square law distance attenuation to predict biological ocular cataract risks and correlate 2.4 GHz WiFi and Bluetooth packet dropouts."
  },
  {
    question: "How does the Slow Cooker Glaze Leaching & Spore Incubation Simulator model risk?",
    answer: "The simulator implements Fickian diffusion and acid chelation kinetics to estimate lead (Pb) and cadmium (Cd) extraction from ceramic glazes against FDA CPG Sec 545.450 limits and California Prop 65 daily thresholds. It simultaneously evaluates thermal dwell times inside the 40°F–140°F (4°C–60°C) danger zone to model Clostridium perfringens and Bacillus cereus endospore germination, while warning of the 5-fold toxicity surge of raw kidney bean phytohaemagglutinin (PHA) at sub-boiling slow cooker temperatures."
  },
  {
    question: "How does the Sous Vide Plastic Migration & Botulinum Safety Modeler calculate food safety?",
    answer: "The modeler solves Fourier thermal conduction equations (Baldwin kinetics) to determine the time required for heat to reach the center (cold spot) of food slabs. It pairs core temperatures with USDA-FSIS D-value lethality tables to verify 6-log10 Listeria and Salmonella pasteurization, while calculating anaerobic Clostridium botulinum neurotoxin proliferation risks for cooks held under 130°F (54.4°C) for over 2 hours."
  },
  {
    question: "How does the Culinary Oil Smoke Point Simulator predict carcinogenic aldehyde formation?",
    answer: "The simulator implements lipid peroxidation kinetics and Arrhenius thermal degradation across 20 culinary fats. It accounts for fatty acid unsaturation ratios (SFA vs MUFA vs PUFA), natural antioxidant polyphenol suppression (ppm), and continuous heating or reuse cycles to quantify Total Polar Materials (TPM) against EU 24% discard limits and calculate cytotoxic 4-HNE, MDA, and volatile acrolein plume emissions."
  },
  {
    question: "How does the Childhood Kitchen Safety & Accidental Toxic Ingestion Evaluator provide triage?",
    answer: "The evaluator stratifies pediatric emergency risk across dishwasher detergent pods, button lithium batteries, rare-earth magnets, and caustic cleaners using America's Poison Centers (AAPCC) and American Academy of Pediatrics (AAP) protocols. It provides instant first-aid directives (such as the Honey Protocol for button batteries), highlights strict contraindications (never induce vomiting), and includes an 8-question CPSC childproofing audit."
  },
  {
    question: "How does the Commercial Cookware NSF Inspector audit equipment safety?",
    answer: "The inspector benchmarks restaurant-grade cookware, cutting boards, and food prep containers against NSF/ANSI Standard 2 (cleanability/welds), Standard 51 (material extraction), and FDA Food Code § 4-101.11. It computes bacterial biofilm harboring risks (0-100%) and chemical sanitizer degradation across commercial warewashing cycles."
  },
  {
    question: "How does the Food Contact Chemical Migration Predictor simulate leaching?",
    answer: "The predictor solves Fick's Second Law of planar diffusion using Arrhenius temperature activation kinetics across 8 material classes and 4 standardized food simulants (EU 10/2011 & US FDA). It models concentration curves C(t) over time to predict the exact moment a migrant crosses regulatory Specific Migration Limits (SML)."
  },
  {
    question: "How does the Smart Kitchen Energy & Carbon Calculator calculate savings?",
    answer: "The calculator models thermodynamic heat transfer efficiency (kWh draw, thermal mass, and cavity losses) across 10 appliances based on DOE 10 CFR 430 and ENERGY STAR v7.0 testing protocols. It applies localized regional electric grid carbon intensity factors (g CO2eq/kWh) and utility rates to project exact financial savings and greenhouse gas abatement."
  },
  {
    question: "How does the Appliance Thermal Shock Simulator determine shatter thresholds?",
    answer: "The simulator solves the thermoelastic stress equation σ = (E · α · ΔT) / (1 - ν) for 6 cookware materials using peer-reviewed coefficients of thermal expansion (CTE) and contact thermal conductivity to predict tensile breaking thresholds and acoustic explosion levels."
  },
  {
    question: "How does the Viral Kitchen Trend Debunker evaluate social media hacks?",
    answer: "The debunker analyzes viral videos from TikTok, Reels, and YouTube Shorts against fundamental physics, thermodynamics, fluid dynamics, and FDA/USDA food safety protocols to calculate a 0-100 Danger Rating and provide safe culinary alternatives."
  },
  {
    question: "How does the Kitchenware Toxic Leaching & PFAS Risk Scorecard calculate danger levels?",
    answer: "The scorecard uses peer-reviewed chemical kinetics (Arrhenius temperature acceleration, acid pH chelation rates, and mechanical microplastic shedding data) to calculate a 0-100 toxicity migration index for 10 common cookware materials."
  },
  {
    question: "Do you store or upload photos taken with the Pan Scratch Inspector?",
    answer: "No. All image processing and optical analysis runs locally in your browser using client-side HTML5 canvas algorithms. Your photos never leave your device."
  },
  {
    question: "How does the Barcode & Product Recalls Scanner check safety records?",
    answer: "The scanner queries our cross-verified database of official Consumer Product Safety Commission (CPSC), FDA, Health Canada, and EU RAPEX recall dockets by product barcode (UPC-A / EAN-13), appliance model number, or brand."
  },
  {
    question: "How often is the Cookware Brand Transparency Index updated?",
    answer: "The brand index is updated continuously as third-party lab audits (SGS, TÜV Rheinland, Intertek) and California Proposition 65 settlement dockets are published."
  },
  {
    question: "What should I do if a kitchen emergency is actively escalating?",
    answer: "If fire escapes an appliance, thick toxic smoke fills the room, or someone has inhaled severe chemical vapors, immediately evacuate all occupants and dial 911 (or local emergency dispatch). Never attempt to fight an out-of-control fire without professional equipment."
  }
];
---

<Layout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} faqs={faqs} availableLocales={['en', 'es', 'pt', 'zh-cn', 'ja']}>
  <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
  <div class="bg-surface-soft border-b border-hairline py-1">
    <div class="max-w-[1280px] mx-auto px-6">
      <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} className="mb-0" />
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="max-w-[1280px] mx-auto px-6 py-10 md:py-16">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="max-w-3xl mb-12">
      <span class="text-caption text-muted uppercase tracking-wider text-xs block mb-2">
        Diagnostic Calculators &bull; Interactive Checkers &bull; Emergency Triage
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-display-lg md:text-display-xl font-medium text-ink tracking-tight mb-4">
        Interactive Kitchen Safety Tools
      </h1>
      <p class="text-body-md text-muted text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed">
        Science-backed diagnostic tools designed to help you verify cookware safety, detect microplastic risks, decode manufacturer marketing claims, and respond immediately to kitchen hazards.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Tools Grid -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 mb-16">
      <!-- Tool 1: AI Pan Scratch Inspector -->
      <article class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-7 flex flex-col justify-between shadow-xs hover:shadow-md transition-all">
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-4">
            <span class="inline-block px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-signature-coral text-white">
              Optical AI Diagnostic
            </span>
            <span class="text-xs text-muted font-mono">Peer-Reviewed Raman</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-title-lg font-medium text-ink tracking-tight mb-3">
            AI Pan Scratch &amp; Damage Inspector
          </h2>
          <p class="text-body text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6">
            Upload a photo of your scratched Teflon or ceramic non-stick skillet. Our browser-based optical contrast scanner detects coating degradation, estimates microplastic particle shedding (from &lt;100 to 2.3M nanoplastics), and provides an instant safety triage grade.
          </p>

          <div class="space-y-2 text-xs mb-6 border-y border-hairline/60 py-3">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Analysis Technology:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">Client-Side Canvas Luminance</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Scientific Basis:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">Newcastle &amp; Flinders (2022)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Privacy:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">100% Local (No Uploads)</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <a 
          href="/tools/pan-scratch-inspector/" 
          class="w-full py-3 px-4 rounded-xl bg-ink hover:bg-black text-white text-center font-medium text-sm transition-colors shadow-xs"
        >
          Launch Pan Scratch Inspector &rarr;
        </a>
      </article>

      <!-- Tool 2: Cookware Brand Transparency Index -->
      <article class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-7 flex flex-col justify-between shadow-xs hover:shadow-md transition-all">
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-4">
            <span class="inline-block px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-emerald-700 text-white">
              Consumer Safety Benchmark
            </span>
            <span class="text-xs text-muted font-mono">25 Brands Audited</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-title-lg font-medium text-ink tracking-tight mb-3">
            Cookware Brand Transparency Index
          </h2>
          <p class="text-body text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6">
            Search 25 top global cookware brands (HexClad, Caraway, GreenPan, Lodge, All-Clad, T-fal, Ninja, and more) to uncover hidden PTFE fluoropolymers, review third-party laboratory leaching audits, and decode deceptive 'PFOA-free' or 'granite' marketing claims.
          </p>

          <div class="space-y-2 text-xs mb-6 border-y border-hairline/60 py-3">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Scope of Audit:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">PFAS, Sol-Gel, Cast Iron, Enamel</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Lab Standards:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">ISO 4531, FDA 21 CFR, Prop 65</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Greenwash Detection:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">8 Brands Flagged with Alerts</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <a 
          href="/tools/cookware-brand-transparency-index/" 
          class="w-full py-3 px-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-700 hover:bg-emerald-800 text-white text-center font-medium text-sm transition-colors shadow-xs"
        >
          Explore Brand Index &rarr;
        </a>
      </article>

      <!-- Tool 3: Kitchen Hazard Emergency Triage -->
      <article class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-7 flex flex-col justify-between shadow-xs hover:shadow-md transition-all">
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-4">
            <span class="inline-block px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-red-600 text-white">
              Emergency Response
            </span>
            <span class="text-xs text-muted font-mono">12 Critical Protocols</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-title-lg font-medium text-ink tracking-tight mb-3">
            Kitchen Hazard Emergency Triage Tool
          </h2>
          <p class="text-body text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6">
            Instant step-by-step emergency triage for sparking microwaves, oven grease fires, thermal shock exploding pyrex, toxic Teflon fumes, and dishwasher suds floods. Includes interactive containment checklists and life-saving prohibitions.
          </p>

          <div class="space-y-2 text-xs mb-6 border-y border-hairline/60 py-3">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Appliance Scope:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">Microwave, Oven, Dishwasher, Fridge</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Fire Standards:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">NFPA 96, UL 923, CDC / NIOSH</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Features:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">Interactive Checklist + Damage Triage</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <a 
          href="/tools/kitchen-hazard-emergency-triage/" 
          class="w-full py-3 px-4 rounded-xl bg-red-600 hover:bg-red-700 text-white text-center font-medium text-sm transition-colors shadow-xs"
        >
          Launch Emergency Triage Tool &rarr;
        </a>
      </article>

      <!-- Tool 4: Barcode & Product Packaging Recalls Scanner -->
      <article class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-7 flex flex-col justify-between shadow-xs hover:shadow-md transition-all">
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-4">
            <span class="inline-block px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-rose-600 text-white">
              Recall Diagnostic Scanner
            </span>
            <span class="text-xs text-muted font-mono">CPSC &bull; FDA &bull; RAPEX</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-title-lg font-medium text-ink tracking-tight mb-3">
            Barcode &amp; Product Recalls Scanner
          </h2>
          <p class="text-body text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6">
            Scan product barcodes with your camera or search model numbers against official CPSC, FDA, and Health Canada recall registries. Verify exploding air fryers, lead-glazed ceramics, defective blender blades, and pressure cooker lid detachments.
          </p>

          <div class="space-y-2 text-xs mb-6 border-y border-hairline/60 py-3">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Database Scope:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">20 Critical Kitchenware Recalls</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Input Modes:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">Camera Barcode + Model Number Search</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Regulatory Coverage:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">CPSC, FDA, Health Canada, EU RAPEX</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <a 
          href="/tools/product-recalls-scanner/" 
          class="w-full py-3 px-4 rounded-xl bg-rose-600 hover:bg-rose-700 text-white text-center font-medium text-sm transition-colors shadow-xs"
        >
          Launch Recalls Scanner &rarr;
        </a>
      </article>

      <!-- Tool 5: Kitchenware Toxic Leaching & PFAS Risk Scorecard -->
      <article class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-7 flex flex-col justify-between shadow-xs hover:shadow-md transition-all">
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-4">
            <span class="inline-block px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-rose-600 text-white">
              Toxicology Diagnostic
            </span>
            <span class="text-xs text-muted font-mono">Heavy Metals &bull; PFAS</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-title-lg font-medium text-ink tracking-tight mb-3">
            Kitchenware Toxic Leaching &amp; PFAS Scorecard
          </h2>
          <p class="text-body text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6">
            Calculate chemical leaching risks and microplastic particle shedding for your cookware. Assess heavy metals (lead, cadmium, aluminum), PFAS fluoropolymer breakdown, and siloxanes based on scratch wear, cooking heat, and food acidity.
          </p>

          <div class="space-y-2 text-xs mb-6 border-y border-hairline/60 py-3">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Materials Covered:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">PTFE, Sol-Gel, Cast Iron, Aluminum, Silicone</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Diagnostic Factors:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">Scratch Wear, Temp, Acidity (pH), Time</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Regulatory Basis:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">FDA 21 CFR, EFSA Contam, ISO 6486</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <a 
          href="/tools/toxic-leaching-scorecard/" 
          class="w-full py-3 px-4 rounded-xl bg-rose-600 hover:bg-rose-700 text-white text-center font-medium text-sm transition-colors shadow-xs"
        >
          Launch Toxicity Scorecard &rarr;
        </a>
      </article>

      <!-- Tool 6: Safe Kitchenware Material Swap Calculator -->
      <article class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-7 flex flex-col justify-between shadow-xs hover:shadow-md transition-all">
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-4">
            <span class="inline-block px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-emerald-700 text-white">
              Non-Toxic Upgrade Engine
            </span>
            <span class="text-xs text-muted font-mono">Zero PFAS &bull; 10-Yr Savings</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-title-lg font-medium text-ink tracking-tight mb-3">
            Safe Kitchenware Material Swap Calculator
          </h2>
          <p class="text-body text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6">
            Replace peeling Teflon, reactive bare aluminum, and plastic containers with certified non-toxic alternatives. Compare stainless steel, cast iron, carbon steel, and glass with verified brand recommendations and 10-year savings.
          </p>

          <div class="space-y-2 text-xs mb-6 border-y border-hairline/60 py-3">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Swaps Covered:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">Teflon, Aluminum, Plastic Storage, Boards</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Safe Materials:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">316 Stainless, Cast Iron, Carbon Steel, Glass</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Lifetime Value:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">Amortized Savings &amp; Microplastics Avoided</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <a 
          href="/tools/material-swap-calculator/" 
          class="w-full py-3 px-4 rounded-xl bg-emerald-700 hover:bg-emerald-800 text-white text-center font-medium text-sm transition-colors shadow-xs"
        >
          Launch Material Swap Calculator &rarr;
        </a>
      </article>

      <!-- Tool 7: Viral Kitchen Trend Debunker -->
      <article class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-7 flex flex-col justify-between shadow-xs hover:shadow-md transition-all">
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-4">
            <span class="inline-block px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-signature-coral text-white">
              Social Media Fact-Checker
            </span>
            <span class="text-xs text-muted font-mono">16 Hacks Tested</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-title-lg font-medium text-ink tracking-tight mb-3">
            Viral Kitchen Trend Debunker
          </h2>
          <p class="text-body text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6">
            Scientific laboratory investigations debunking viral TikTok, Instagram Reels, and YouTube kitchen hacks. Verify the thermal shock, fire risks, and explosion hazards of microwave eggs, dishwasher salmon, and sideways toasters.
          </p>

          <div class="space-y-2 text-xs mb-6 border-y border-hairline/60 py-3">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Platform Coverage:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">TikTok, Reels, YouTube Shorts</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Scientific Scope:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">Superheating, Thermal Shock, NFPA Fire</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Key Features:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">Danger Index + Safe Alternatives</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <a 
          href="/tools/viral-trend-debunker/" 
          class="w-full py-3 px-4 rounded-xl bg-ink hover:bg-black text-white text-center font-medium text-sm transition-colors shadow-xs"
        >
          Launch Viral Trend Debunker &rarr;
        </a>
      </article>

      <!-- Tool 8: Appliance Thermal Shock & Shatter Threshold Safety Simulator -->
      <article class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-7 flex flex-col justify-between shadow-xs hover:shadow-md transition-all">
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-4">
            <span class="inline-block px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-indigo-600 text-white">
              Thermodynamic Simulator
            </span>
            <span class="text-xs text-muted font-mono">ASTM C149 &bull; ISO 3585</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-title-lg font-medium text-ink tracking-tight mb-3">
            Appliance Thermal Shock &amp; Shatter Threshold Safety Simulator
          </h2>
          <p class="text-body text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6">
            Simulate sudden temperature swings (ΔT) across tempered soda-lime glass, vintage borosilicate, ceramic stoneware, and enameled cast iron. Calculate tensile breaking stress, acoustic shockwave risk, and explosive shatter thresholds before moving hot dishes.
          </p>

          <div class="space-y-2 text-xs mb-6 border-y border-hairline/60 py-3">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Physics Engine:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">Thermoelastic σ = (E·α·ΔT)/(1-ν)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Materials Covered:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">6 Substrates (Soda-Lime, Borosilicate, etc.)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Key Diagnostics:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">Dynamic SVG Cracking + Acoustic dB</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <a 
          href="/tools/thermal-shock-simulator/" 
          class="w-full py-3 px-4 rounded-xl bg-ink hover:bg-black text-white text-center font-medium text-sm transition-colors shadow-xs"
        >
          Launch Thermal Shock Simulator &rarr;
        </a>
      </article>

      <!-- Tool 9: Smart Kitchen Energy & Appliance Carbon Footprint Calculator -->
      <article class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-7 flex flex-col justify-between shadow-xs hover:shadow-md transition-all">
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-4">
            <span class="inline-block px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-emerald-600 text-white">
              Thermodynamic Energy Engine
            </span>
            <span class="text-xs text-muted font-mono">DOE 10 CFR 430 &bull; ENERGY STAR</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-title-lg font-medium text-ink tracking-tight mb-3">
            Smart Kitchen Energy &amp; Appliance Carbon Footprint Calculator
          </h2>
          <p class="text-body text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6">
            Compare exact kilowatt-hour (kWh) electricity draw, cooking durations, utility costs, and greenhouse gas emissions across induction, air fryer, microwave, standard oven, and gas cooktops. Calculate your annual carbon abatement and dollar savings instantly.
          </p>

          <div class="space-y-2 text-xs mb-6 border-y border-hairline/60 py-3">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Calculations Engine:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">DOE Testing Protocols &bull; Regional Grid Factors</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Appliances Audited:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">10 Appliance Classes (Induction, Air Fryer, etc.)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="text-muted">Impact Metrics:</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink">Annual $ Saved, CO₂ Abated &bull; Air Quality Index</span>
            </div>
          </div>
